@@ -0,0 +1,40 @@
+---
+id: dl-007-rentals-shorter-than-a-day-are-priced-by-the-hour
+type: decision-log
+title: "Rentals shorter than a day are priced by the hour"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+## Context
+
+Many visitors want a board for an afternoon, and the desk turns them away because the shortest rental is
+a whole day. The brief asks for rentals by the hour: an item has an optional hourly price, and a rental
+shorter than a day that starts and ends on the hour is priced per hour. An item without an hourly price
+cannot be rented by the hour. This partly changes dl-001 (whole-day periods) and dl-002 (midnight-only
+times).
+
+## Decision
+
+- `addEquipment` takes an optional `hourlyPrice`, in integer euro cents, validated like `dailyPrice`
+  (a non-negative safe integer, zero accepted). Without it the item is daily-only.
+- A period shorter than 24 hours whose `start` and `end` are whole UTC hours (`YYYY-MM-DDTHH:00:00Z`,
+  optionally with `.000`) is an hourly rental. Its total is `hourlyPrice` times the number of hours. It
+  may cross midnight, such as 23:00 to 01:00.
+- A period of 24 hours or more keeps the whole-day rule of dl-001: `start` and `end` must be UTC midnights.
+- An hourly rental of an item with no hourly price is refused by `quote` and `book`.
+- An hourly rental is never discounted: it is shorter than the 3-day threshold of dl-006.
+- Overlap is checked on the exact instants, so an hourly booking conflicts with any booking it overlaps,
+  including a whole-day one. Back-to-back periods are still allowed.
+- `availability` accepts hourly periods, with the same validation as `quote` and `book`. It lists the free
+  items whatever their hourly price; it does not check that an item can be rented by the hour.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- dl-002's rule that times are midnight UTC now applies only to periods of 24 hours or more. Sub-day
+  periods may use whole hours. Offsets, minutes and seconds are still refused.
+- An item with no hourly price keeps its previous behaviour: a sub-day period on the hour is refused.
+- `availability` can list an item as free for an hour that it cannot be rented for, when it has no
+  hourly price. A caller that needs rentable items only must check the hourly price separately. This is a
+  choice to revisit if the desk wants `availability` to filter by rentability.
+- Bookings are in memory, so the change needs no migration.
